</table>

<!-- ===================================================== 15 -->
<h2>15. Rules and gotchas that decide whether a trigger plays</h2>
<ol>
  <li><b>One trigger per frame.</b> Two view-model triggers fired in the same frame: only one is consumed. Everything here spaces them: Hex queue 150 ms, robot clip length + 150 ms, strike 150 ms after correct/wrong, battery <code>gain</code> and <code>fullFlash</code> 150 ms apart.</li>
  <li><b>Trigger while a move plays is dropped.</b> The robot only takes the next trigger once its state machine is back at rest, hence the queue and the per-move lengths in <code>moveSeconds</code>. If an animation clip length in the .riv changes, <code>moveSeconds</code> must change with it.</li>
  <li><b>First trigger after load is dropped</b> (robot: 600 ms settle). Hex's first trigger is <code>enter</code>, queued after the machine is played and bound.</li>
  <li><b>A new machine is not bound automatically.</b> After every <code>play(state)</code> Hex rebinds the view model instance.</li>
  <li><b><code>entryStyle</code> must be set before <code>enter</code>.</b> The hook does this for every new <code>entryKey</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Null <code>entryKey</code> = waiting.</b> The result panel mounts its Hex canvas while closed (null key) so the file is already loaded; the entrance plays only when the key arrives.</li>
  <li><b><code>fireNow</code> clears the queue.</b> Cues and exits use it so nothing queued (talk, ambient idle) can delay or override them. The side effect: anything queued is lost.</li>
  <li><b>Talk must be ended.</b> The hook inserts <code>stopTalk</code> before any non-talk trigger; the component fires it when the voice ends.</li>
  <li><b>Property writes do not repaint a still artboard.</b> The button and label writers call <code>drawFrame()</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Resizing a canvas clears it.</b> The button debounces its resize 100 ms; the progress bar cuts with CSS instead of resizing; the battery pins its frame instead of resizing the bitmap.</li>
  <li><b>Hot reload creates a second instance.</b> The hosts decline hot updates for this reason.</li>
  <li><b>Persistent canvases survive navigation only in the browser.</b> Hosts are module-level singletons; <code>getRobotHost</code>, <code>getModuleButtonHost</code>, <code>getProgressBarHost</code> and <code>getBatteryHost</code> are browser-only.</li>
  <li><b>Reduced motion.</b> Within the module's screens, only the examples carousel (screen 14) honours <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> (no auto-advance, full countdown fill); a global rule in <code>globals.css</code> also disables page view-transition animations. The Rive animations (Hex, robot, strikes) and framer-motion springs are not switched off for it.</li>
</ol>

<p class="meta">End of document.</p>
</body>
</html>
